6-501.111 Controlling Pests.
The PREMISES shall be maintained free of insects, rodents, and other pests. The presence of insects, rodents, and other pests shall be controlled to eliminate their presence on the PREMISES by:
(A) Routinely inspecting incoming shipments of FOOD and supplies;
(B) Routinely inspecting the PREMISES for evidence of pests;
(C) Using methods, if pests are found, such as trapping devices or other means of pest control as specified under §§ 7-202.12, 7-206.12, and 7-206.13; Pf and
(D) Eliminating harborage conditions.

750.100 - Several canned foods (14 total) with severe dents and/or damage to the top/bottom/side seams were observed stocked on the shelves for sale. Products included the following:
1) MW Polar Foods - peach slices (2 cans; 15.25oz);
2) Pampa - strawberries (1 can; 15oz);
3) Campbell's - chicken noodle soup (4 cans; 14.75oz);
4) Kendale Farm - cream of mushroom soup (1 can; 14.5oz);
5) Libby's - french style green beans (1 can; 14.5oz);
6) Libby's - sliced beets  (1 can; 15oz);
7) Libby's - sweet peas (1 can; `5oz);
8) Bruce's - yams (1 can 20oz);
9) Libby's - whole white potatoes (1 can; 15oz);   and
10) Goya - small red beans (1 can; 15.5oz).
Products were removed to be inventoried and discarded.

Food shall be in sound condition, free from spoilage, filth, and other contamination and shall be safe for human consumption. **Cans with dents along any of the seams, severe dents anywhere on the can, rust, or evidence of bulging must not be stocked for sale. Refuse questionable products upon receiving a shipment, when possible. Otherwise, set aside damaged products during stocking and do not stock for sale**
